  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\sqrt{2} \\int \\frac{\\sin x d x}{\\sin \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)}=\\sqrt{2} \\int \\frac{\\sin \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) d x}{\\sin \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)} \\\\\n& =\\sqrt{2} \\int\\left(\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\cot \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) d x \\\\\n& =\\int d x+\\int \\cot \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) d x \\\\\n& =x+\\ln \\left|\\sin \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right|+c .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
